# Example Project CLAUDE.md

This is what `/init-harness` generates for a typical TypeScript backend project.
Your actual CLAUDE.md will differ based on project analysis.

---

## Build

```bash
npm run dev          # Start dev server
npm run build        # Production build
npm run test         # Run tests (vitest)
npm run lint         # ESLint + Prettier check
npm run typecheck    # tsc --noEmit
```

## Architecture

- src/modules/{domain}/ — feature modules (controller, service, repository)
- Dependency direction: controller → service → repository (never reverse)
- No direct DB access from controllers
- All external calls wrapped in service layer

## Conventions

- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Error handling: custom AppError class, centralized error handler
- Naming: camelCase for variables/functions, PascalCase for types/classes
- Tests colocated: `src/modules/user/user.service.test.ts`

## Harness

### Agent Routing
- Users do not need to name harness skills.
- Ordinary feature work stays ordinary.
- "This keeps failing", "stop repeating this", or "make this not happen again" routes to harness-engineer.
- "Review this carefully" or "am I missing anything?" routes to multi-review when risk warrants it.
- "Try variants", "optimize this", or "keep the measurable winner" routes to autoresearch only with a fixed evaluator and clear metric.
- "Did the harness learn from this?" or "check for dogfood gaps" routes to bounded dogfood review: propose trace/search-set/instruction candidates only when a concrete trigger-evidence pointer, reusable future value, and a clear next action are all present.

### Hooks (`.claude/settings.local.json`)
- PostToolUse Edit|Write on `*.ts` → `tsc --noEmit` (blocking)
- PostToolUse Edit|Write on `*.test.ts` → `vitest run --reporter=verbose` (blocking)

### Traces
- Active trace root: `.claude/traces/` (single root; if this project uses git
  worktrees, replace this with the shared absolute or migrated root used by
  every worktree)
- `.claude/traces/evolution/` — harness change history
- `.claude/traces/failures/` — failure diagnosis (YAML: classification, resolved)
- `.claude/traces/search-set.md` — verification cases
- The global Claude trace root at `${CLAUDE_HOME:-~/.claude}/harness/traces` is
  cross-project agent memory only. It can record routing/install/profile-drift
  mistakes that span projects, but it does not replace this project's active
  trace root or search-set guards.
- Harness-changing trace claims use `retrieval.mode` plus byte-matching
  `raw_trace_refs`; trace catalogs are retrieval pointers, not evidence.
- Bounded self-evolution proposals are diagnostic until adopted. Do not
  auto-edit Active search-set entries or treat low trace volume as failure.

### Failure Recording
Record a non-obvious operational workaround with reusable future value even
when the immediate task succeeds. Examples: cwd drift that changes command
paths, orphaned dev-server cleanup, sandbox/permission/network recovery, and
session-state drift. Do not record simple typos, obvious one-offs, one-off CLI
deprecations, agent-created verification mistakes, or use a numeric
corrective-round threshold.

### Change Strategy
Additive first → Subtractive → Structural. One change at a time.
Record all changes in `.claude/traces/evolution/` with verdict.
